825 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 394 0 R
/E (Four species of the Plasmodium parasites are responsible for human malaria infection - P.falciparum, P.vivax, P.ovale and P.malariae. P.falciparum and P.vivax are the most prevalent . Falciparum infection is associated with Cerebral malaria and drug resistance whereas vivax infection is associated with high rate of infectivity and relapse. Differentiation between P.falciparum and P.vivax is of utmost importance for better patient management and speedy recovery.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [24]
>>
